    "result_text": "I've added the policy date setting. `bin/e2e` builds the app and all 4 tests in the spec pass.\n\n**How it behaves**\n- A claim dated before the policy date rounds half up. A claim dated on or after it rounds half to even. This applies to both the rate step and the late charge.\n- A correction rounds by the date of the claim it corrects, not its own date. Half up rounds away from zero, so a correction of \u22121.025 shows \u22121.03.\n- Settled and statement-bound figures are stored values, so they don't change when the policy date does.\n\n**Server**\n- **New `setting/PolicyDate.java`:** works out the policy date, using the sheet's today when the setting is blank. It also decides how each claim rounds, finding a corrected claim by its number within the same person's claims.\n- **Where rounding happens:** the four places that rounded figures now use that decision instead of always rounding half to even: `Rollup`, `TakeStatement`, `ApplyClaimAction` (when settling) and `LatePct` (the late charge).\n- **Settings:** the server now accepts `policy-date` as either blank or a `yyyy-MM-dd` date and refuses anything else. The settings list returns it, blank until set.\n- **Audit:** saving the setting writes `SETTING_CHANGED ... key=policy-date value=<date>`. The settings save already writes ROLLUP/TOTALS lines when a figure changes, so I added nothing there.\n- **Database:** no migration was needed, because settings are already stored as key/value rows.\n\n**Front end**\n- The Settings form has a new \"Policy date\" field (`setting-policy-date`, with `setting-policy-date-current` showing the saved value).\n- The screen applies the same rounding rule, so the due figures it shows match the server's.\n\nWhen the policy date is blank, moving the sheet's today can change how open claims round. Saving a new today already writes ROLLUP lines for any figures that move.",
